{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is a rectangle. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is outside the rectangle so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349d6d9248df6b07ce3f534750bfe29606cb7c8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PTQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is an isosceles right-angled triangle with hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbbdd6e7a8ba9069dc0308e2f4e0885a3a3eca94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9090513924b0ec678c06928c45e75f310b9572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, then the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c859c9c8b9daf236f97a00f84def850038ecf1fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PTR$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99fd6a7a5e27d46b8c92c597ff74fe3ccc39d03f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;);  defaultpen(TimesRoman()); defaultpen(linewidth(1.2bp));  size(125);  pair P = (2,0); pair Q = (2,4); pair R = (5,4); pair SPoint = (5,0); pair T = (0,2);  draw(P--Q--R--SPoint--cycle); draw(R--P); draw(Q--T); draw(R--T); draw(P--T);  label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, SW); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, Q, N); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, R, NE); label(&quot;$T$&quot;, T, W); label(&quot;$S$&quot;, SPoint, SE); [/asy]\" width=\"208\" height=\"182\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58c86f7c7192f792729ab40f60cc53ae3815d92c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   5  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   6  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   7  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   8  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   9  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"384\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349d6d9248df6b07ce3f534750bfe29606cb7c8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PTQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is an isosceles right triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/15230b3cf4369d9876eda1b92d07481040d14c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QT = TP = \\frac{PQ}{\\sqrt{2}} = 2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"195\" height=\"44\" />. Further, we can decompose the area of the entire polygon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e50654d1ebf7b26e1ac52de9d87459cda8658e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PTQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> in two ways:\n\\begin{align}\n\t[PTQRS] &amp;= [PTQ] + [PQRS] = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot QT\\cdot TP  + PQ\\cdot QR = 18\\\\\n\t        &amp;= [QTR] + [PTR] + [PRS]\n\\end{align}\nThe height from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/61730fee7c7b702a13e070cc84f493ffd07af78b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle QTR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d6ce156be289821b3532a6b583ef70f75cb5ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot PQ = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d8d0f0b7667e1b694e3423265872c4e98a0968.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[QTR] = \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot QR \\cdot 2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"188\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c60cbae221adc46ebdc3f5fe334083a4df3c793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[PRS] = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot PS \\cdot SR = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot QR \\cdot PQ = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"322\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc234db86c138804de2be4c3875a6d89b3cd587.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[PTR] = 16 - [QTR] - [PRS] = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\   7}\\]\" width=\"317\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.p